{"id":"spell.invocation-command-halt-grovel","title":"Spell invocation records failed-save Command Grovel and Halt pending effects and resolves them at the target turn","profileKind":"spell-invocation","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/battle-discovery.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/dispatcher.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/turn-end-movement.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/unit-profile-admission.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV50A","SRDINV50B"],"sourceBoundary":"This profile supports Command's cast shell, slot-scaled creature target list, Wisdom save, and the Grovel and Halt options. Drop is represented by spell.invocation-command-drop-held-object; Approach is represented by spell.invocation-command-approach-route; Flee is represented by spell.invocation-command-flee-route."}
{"id":"spell.invocation-command-drop-held-object","title":"Spell invocation resolves Command Drop through held-object facts and dropped-object outcomes","profileKind":"table-caller","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/battle-discovery.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/dispatcher.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/turn-end-movement.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/unit-profile-admission.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV50C"],"sourceBoundary":"This profile supports Command Drop by consuming canonical character loadout held-object facts when present or caller-supplied held-object facts otherwise, emitting dropped-object outcomes, and ending the target turn. It does not add general inventory simulation, object placement, or loadout mutation."}
{"id":"spell.invocation-command-approach-route","title":"Spell invocation resolves Command Approach through caller-supplied shortest-direct-route movement facts","profileKind":"table-caller","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/battle-discovery.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/dispatcher.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/turn-end-movement.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/unit-profile-admission.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV50D1"],"sourceBoundary":"This profile supports Command Approach by consuming caller-supplied route/proximity facts on the existing Movement fill when movement is available, spending the target's movement through the normal movement reducer, and ending the target turn only when that supplied route reaches within 5 feet of the caster. If the target has no available movement, it clears the pending Approach effect without ending the turn. It does not add pathfinding or route storage."}
{"id":"spell.invocation-command-flee-route","title":"Spell invocation resolves Command Flee through caller-supplied fastest-available moving-away route facts","profileKind":"table-caller","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/battle-discovery.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/dispatcher.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/turn-end-movement.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/unit-profile-admission.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV50D2"],"sourceBoundary":"This profile supports Command Flee by consuming caller-supplied fastest-available moving-away route facts on the existing Movement fill, requiring the selected remaining Movement budget to be spent when movement is available, clearing the pending effect, and ending the target turn. If the target has no available movement, it clears the pending Flee effect and ends the turn without a Movement fill. Opportunity Attack eligibility is derived from the Movement fill's actual provoked-threat facts, not from Command route metadata. It does not add pathfinding, route storage, or route choice AI."}
{"id":"spell.invocation-expeditious-retreat-dash","title":"Spell invocation immediately resolves Dash and grants Concentration-owned Bonus Action Dash","profileKind":"spell-invocation","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/unit-profile-admission.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV49"],"sourceBoundary":"Movement budget updates reuse the battle Dash/action owner; the spell effect stores only the Concentration-owned permission to take Dash as a Bonus Action."}
{"id":"spell.invocation-feather-fall-mitigation","title":"Spell invocation reacts to falling creatures with per-target Feather Fall mitigation","profileKind":"spell-invocation","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/dispatcher.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/reaction-triggered-spells.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/feather-fall-reaction-spell.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV56A","SRDINV56B"],"sourceBoundary":"The runtime consumes caller-supplied falling trigger and falling target facts, spends the caster's Reaction and Spell Slot, admits up to five falling targets within range, creates one-minute per-target mitigation effects, exposes the 60-foot descent-rate cap projection, and consumes caller-supplied landing facts to clear the landed target's mitigation while emitting fall-damage prevention and Falling-Prone prevention outcomes. Fall-distance derivation, map elevation, and landing geometry remain caller/table-owned."}
{"id":"spell.reaction-hellish-rebuke","title":"Reaction spell opens Hellish Rebuke after-damage casting window","profileKind":"reaction","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/dispatcher.ts","packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer/reaction-triggered-spells.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/hellish-rebuke-reaction-spell.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV69A","SRDINV69B"],"sourceBoundary":"The runtime consumes caller-supplied after-damage facts establishing that the damaged reactor took damage from a visible creature within 60 feet, requires Hellish Rebuke spell access, an available Reaction, and an available Spell Slot, then opens an after-damage Reaction frame carrying the damager, damaged reactor, and slot-level continuation facts. The continuation resolves through the shared save-gated damage invocation profile."}
