{"id":"spell.invocation-forced-reaction-movement","title":"Spell invocation consumes caller-supplied failed-save Reaction movement facts","profileKind":"spell-invocation","qntOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"],"runtimeOwners":["packages/battle-runtime/src/battle-reducer.ts"],"verificationOwners":[{"kind":"qnt-proof","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/battle-runtime.qnt"},{"kind":"runtime-test","ownerPath":"packages/battle-runtime/src/unit-profile-admission.test.ts"}],"taskRefs":["SRDINV52"],"sourceBoundary":"The runtime consumes Reaction availability, caller-supplied safest-route Movement, and table-supplied Opportunity Attack threats; route/pathfinding geometry is not derived inside the reducer. Package-local Quint models the reducer protocol for Reaction spend, no-movement fallback, Movement fill admission, Opportunity Attack interruption, and after-damage continuation ordering."}
